class:: PitchDeviation
summary:: Signed cents deviation from a reference or tuning grid
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Pitch
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Pitch2, Classes/FundamentalCandidates, Classes/PitchStability, Classes/TuningFrequency

description::
Uses the logarithmic frequency-ratio definition of musical cents. The previous mode compares consecutive control blocks and resets its reference on an unvoiced block. Reference mode accepts a changing frequency, so a custom tuning system can supply its selected reference externally. There is no internal pitch estimation or smoothing.

Vanilla link::Classes/UnaryOpUGen:: frequency-to-MIDI arithmetic can express the same cents conversion. This class also supplies reference/grid/previous policies and explicit undefined-input behavior.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: freq
Control-rate frequency in Hz; invalid or nonpositive values return zero.

argument:: reference
Positive reference in Hz. In nearest12TET mode it anchors the equal-tempered grid; another reference can establish a custom anchor.

argument:: mode
One of \reference (1200 * log2(freq/reference)), \nearest12TET (nearest 100-cent grid point), or \previous (previous control-block frequency).

returns::
Signed deviation in cents. Positive is sharp; negative is flat. Exact half-semitone ties use round-away-from-zero in the grid index.

examples::
PitchDeviation measures signed microtonal pitch deviation in cents against an equal-tempered 12-TET grid or an arbitrary tuning reference. In this example, it drives an adaptive pitch-correction synthesizer: detected cents deviation quantizes a parallel tracking voice into exact 12-TET intonation beside the expressive acoustic source. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: plots the real-time cents deviation ($-50 \dots +50$ cents).
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic melody fallback
            Saw.ar(Select.kr(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(0, 5), [220, 261.63, 293.66, 329.63, 392, 440])) * 0.2
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var pitch = PitchMPM.kr(source, 80, 1200, 2048, 0.25);
        var cents = PitchDeviation.kr(pitch[0], mode: \nearest12TET);
        var snappedFreq = pitch[0] * (cents.neg / 100).midiratio;
        var tunedVoice = SinOsc.ar(snappedFreq.clip(50, 2000).lag(0.02), 0, pitch[1].lag(0.04) * 0.15 * (pitch[0] > 50));
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + tunedVoice;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, cents) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Cents Deviation", ~miraBus, -50.0, 50.0, "cents");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
